  },
  {
    "claim": "The flowlang builder has three verified gaps around FFI library crates (all worked around, all wanting an upstream flow-repo PR): (1) the default generated Cargo.toml declares serde/serde_json optional deps but omits the serde_support/python_runtime/javascript_runtime feature blocks, so any compile passing --features=serde_support fails until the features are added - which is why the agent/kb/scratch/nebula repos track their crate Cargo.tomls by hand; (2) the generated <ctl>/mod.rs cmdinit is append-only across regenerations - stale command ids accumulate (a delete+re-upsert leaves both generations registered) and the built dylib lags the sources by one compile - the clean reset is delete the generated src dir and run `newbound rebuild`; (3) build_lib answers 'unchanged' when a repo's tracked generated src already matches the store, so rebuild_lib skips the crate build and a fresh install never produces an artifact - dev.github.import/update now build the crate unconditionally.",
    "tags": "platform-api,flowlang,builder,ffi,bug",
    "source": {
      "doc": "verified live during the nebula overhaul, 2026-08-09"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786295573656
  },
